{
  "name": "JSRunner",
  "params": {
    "jsPath": "js/smAgent.js",
    "jobParams": {
      "repo": "epam/dmtools-dart",
      "maxTriggeredWorkflows": 3,
      "rules": [
        {
          "description": "Validated-but-stale: armed (ai_validating) + validation concluded but BASE MOVED (BEHIND only). BLOCKED must NOT unarm: since #483 BLOCKED is a real verdict, and on a freshly armed head BLOCKED simply means 'required checks pending' — unarming there races validate-armed in the SAME tick and deadlocks the PR forever (live: fa pr-762 armed at 08:25:37, unarmed 08:25:58 by the BLOCKED match, re-armed next tick, loop). silent-update-behind excludes ai_validating and merge-validated needs CLEAN, so without this unarm a genuinely moved base still deadlocks (live: fa pr-744) — BEHIND-only keeps that recovery and stops the self-inflicted one.",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "mergeState": [
              "BEHIND"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "unarm_validation",
          "limit": 1,
          "id": "unarm-stale-validation"
        },
        {
          "description": "RULE ORDER (dmtools-agents#637 aftermath, live fa pr-1174 2026-10-03): this rule MUST run before sweep-stale-validating — the 15-min staleness sweep eats every arm before the merge can consume it whenever the tick cadence slips past 15 min (night kicker slippage), looping arm→sweep→arm on a green merge-ready head. GitHub PR: validation green + CLEAN -> squash-merge (merge_pr verifies the sticky pr_approved latch on the PR; an un-approved green head latches ai_validated instead — see merge_pr). FIFO drain (#687).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "checks": "green",
            "mergeState": "CLEAN"
          },
          "localAction": "merge_pr",
          "limit": 1,
          "id": "merge-validated"
        },
        {
          "description": "Stale-arm sweeper (live: fa #999 — ai_validating held 7h with a CONCLUDED green CI and no verdict consumed; the ai_validating mutex stayed held forever. unarm-stale-validation covers BEHIND only). ai_validating + the head's dispatched validation run CONCLUDED (success or failure — CANCELLED is never a verdict) more than staleMinutes (15) ago, arm never consumed → unarm. Success side: unarm + re-latch ai_validated (complete_validation parity — the merge window re-flows; validate-armed latch-skips on the unchanged head). Failure side: the standard fail path (report + machine-only rework re-arm). Fresh conclusions (<15 min) never sweep: the check-visibility/verdict race window — the same-tick verdict rules (merge-validated / fail-validation / validated-green) own those. BEHIND excluded: unarm-stale-validation owns the moved-base recovery.",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "notMergeState": [
              "BEHIND"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "sweep_stale_validation",
          "staleMinutes": 15,
          "limit": 10,
          "id": "sweep-stale-validating"
        },
        {
          "description": "Every open non-draft PR behind main gets a silent branch refresh with the workflow token (pushes trigger no workflows, so freshness is free); validating PRs are excluded so the validation head never moves mid-run. mergeState is BEHIND only: the prStatus deterministic override computes BEHIND from base freshness (immune to the REST BEHIND/BLOCKED flip-flop this rule used to paper over with both values), and BLOCKED is now a REAL verdict (fresh head, required checks pending/red) — updating those would no-op-clone every pending PR on every tick. Limit 20 (owner 2026-09-22): silent pushes fire no CI — refreshing every BEHIND head every tick is free and keeps PRs merge-ready, so the merge window never waits for a refresh first. STICKY PARK (owner 2026-09-27, live: fa#923): before refreshing, a GUEST PR whose current head has RED checks is labeled validation_failed (idempotent, the head SHA noted in a one-time comment) — validate-armed excludes the label and no validation CI is dispatched for it at all; the label is REMOVED only when the head's LAST committer is NOT 'sm-silent-update' (an author push), so the SM's own silent-updates never re-arm a red guest. Machine-authored PRs never get the label (fa pushes their heads).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "notLabels": [
              "ai_validating"
            ],
            "mergeState": [
              "BEHIND"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "update_branch",
          "limit": 10,
          "id": "silent-update-behind"
        },
        {
          "description": "Sticky-park RESET for NON-BEHIND heads (dmtools-agents, live fa 2026-10-03): the human-push unpark probe lives inside update_branch, but silent-update-behind only matches mergeState BEHIND — a guest PR whose fix commit lands on the SAME base (not behind) NEVER runs the RESET and the park outlives any human push (live: vendor pushed 16:01 to five parked approved PRs; 2h later not one label cleared, the whole approved FIFO frozen). This rule routes every parked non-validating PR through update_branch's RESET probe regardless of merge state: a NON-machine push NEWER than the newest park event clears the label (then validate-armed picks the PR up on a later pass — this rule never dispatches CI itself); machine pushes and stale heads keep the park (fail closed). The silent branch refresh inside the action is a no-op for a non-BEHIND head (git merge reports up-to-date, no push).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "validation_failed"
            ],
            "notLabels": [
              "ai_validating",
              "blocked"
            ],
            "draft": false
          },
          "localAction": "update_branch",
          "limit": 10,
          "id": "park-reset"
        },
        {
          "description": "Post-approval merge window — OWNER FIFO RULE (2026-09-22): lead the OLDEST approved PR all the way to merge; never validate other approved PRs meanwhile (the merge moves the base — they would re-validate anyway). Advance to the next approved ONLY when the oldest is DIRTY (conflict-rework owns it) or its validation went RED (rework leg fixes it) — both free this slot while the oldest repairs. BEHIND/DIRTY excluded here: silent-update refreshes BEHIND heads first; conflicted heads can never reach CLEAN. Mutex ai_validating = one validation at a time. validation_failed excluded (owner 2026-09-27, live: fa#923 — a GUEST PR whose head went red cycles arm→CI red→silent-update→re-arm forever, holding this limit-1 slot hostage; the silent-update action labels such guests validation_failed and they stay parked until a NON-MACHINE push moves the head).",
          "source": "github",
          "query": {
            "type": "pr",
            "labels": [
              "pr_approved"
            ],
            "notLabels": [
              "ai_validating",
              "validation_failed"
            ],
            "notMergeState": [
              "BEHIND",
              "DIRTY"
            ],
            "draft": false,
            "mutex": "ai_validating",
            "mutexAmong": [
              "pr_approved"
            ]
          },
          "localAction": "validate_pr",
          "skipIfValidatedHead": true,
          "limit": 1,
